messages:
elaine: Heads-up — discovered a reproducible screen-reader jump when navigating the models table with VoiceOver + keyboard. Happens only with virtualization on (infinite scroll). Row receives programmatic focus while VO is speaking, which interrupts reading and moves the rotor. Screenshot + short recording here: https://redwood/internal/clip/rec123 :eyes:

mohit: ugh. yep i've seen similar w/ our log stream component. likely tabindex or focus() being called on mount. can you repro with `data-qa=virtual-row` toggled off?

elaine: repro steps in thread: 1) open Models list 2) keyboard down to row 10 3) wait for virtualized render to bring row 30 into DOM 4) VO stops and jumps to new row. toggling virtualization fixes it.

katie: sounds like we need to avoid calling `.focus()` on mount unless the user invoked a keyboard action that expects focus there. also our focus ring in dark theme for the focused cell is #6b6b6b which fails 4.5:1 on small targets. low contrast + abrupt focus jump = accessibility fail.

sam: quick idea: keep tabindex=-1 on virtual rows and only set tabindex=0 when the user explicitly tabs/arrow-activates that row. avoid programmatic focus during passive renders. fallback: place an offscreen live region that announces "New rows rendered" with `aria-live="polite"` so VO doesn't lose its current element. thoughts? :thinking_face:

mohit: Agree with the tabindex approach. Also note that NVDA behavior differs; it will often preserve virtual cursor if no focus() call happens. So the safest is: stop focus() on mount, and gating tabindex to explicit user action.

elaine: sample change i sketched:

```
// on row mount
if (row.wasKeyboardNavigated) {
  row.element.tabIndex = 0
  // focus only when user pressed arrow key or enter
  if (row.requestFocus) { row.element.focus() }
} else {
  row.element.tabIndex = -1
}
```

katie: + CSS change proposal for focus ring:

```
:root[data-theme="dark"] .table-row:focus {
  outline: 2px solid #cfd8dc; /* meets 4.5:1 on 2px thick */
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```

sam: For screen readers, avoid announcing "New rows rendered" too verbosely. Maybe only announce when the user is at the end of the list and new content is appended (infinite scroll case). Otherwise rely on existing cursor.

a11y-bot: Automated scan results (2026-03-23T14:05): virtualized-table component flagged: 1 high (unexpected focus change), 2 medium (focus contrast), 3 low (missing aria-describedby on pagination controls). Link: https://redwood/internal/a11y/scans/2345

mohit: Plan: 1) revert programmatic focus on mount (hotfix), 2) implement keyboard-nav gating for tabindex (next dev cycle), 3) update focus styles for dark theme (design review), 4) add unit + e2e NVDA/VO smoke tests. Can we ship 1 & 3 as a canary tomorrow?

katie: yes can do the focus style in a patch. i'll PR the tokens + visual tests. also i'll pair with QA on the NVDA checklist (voiceover has slightly different expectations).

elaine: i'll add a short acceptance test to flakey-test-suite: keyboard walk down 50 rows in both themes and assert no focus() calls except when user arrowed. also will capture voiceover recording for regression harness.

sam: Pre-deploy checklist: add note in RELEASE.md: "a11y: virtualized table — removed programmatic focus on mount; tabindex gated to keyboard nav; improved dark theme focus contrast" and notify support for any regressions.

mohit: tagging for review: @katie @sam please skim the change in PR #4821 when it's up. cc @security for the release note (there's no perf impact). :thumbsup:

katie: ack — will review tonight. thanks everyone.

elaine: resolving for now, moving to a short-lived branch `fix/virt-sr-focus` and will post the PR link when ready. :rocket:
